## Purpose
Establish the final provider-neutral routing seam for parallel Browser Brain mutations without adding a scheduler, polling loop, DB authority, or automatic retry.

## Stack
- Base PR: #334 (`work/browser-brain-runtime-fence-v1`)
- Exact source base: `3c14720402702292d720c15be74b22789806d9dd`

## Changes
- add `BrowserBrainExactMutationRouter`;
- require explicit `payload.tab_id` for every mutating native action;
- reuse #334 `prepareMutation()` and `assertMutationTarget()` fences;
- resolve WebContents only by exact tab identity; selected/platform fallback is impossible in this layer;
- assert the runtime fence immediately before the injected physical executor;
- permit concurrent effects across independent BrowserCells;
- fail closed on overlapping same-cell mutation instead of creating a hidden queue/second scheduler;
- never retry failed or ambiguous physical effects.

## Tests
Focused tests prove explicit tab enforcement, assertion-before-effect ordering, cross-cell parallelism, same-cell fail-closed behavior and zero automatic retry.

## Safety
Source-only. No production DDL, Edge deploy, release/cutover, Browser reset/close or live Browser actuation. This PR does not lease commands and does not itself execute any effect until a later wiring slice supplies the existing physical executor.

## What changed

Stacked on #332.

- adds `BrowserBrainRuntimeControlPlane`, composing exact runtime binding, bounded Brain memory and pressure state without adding scheduler/lease authority;
- adds a fail-closed mutation fence over `command_id -> explicit tab -> BrowserCell/binding generation -> WebContents.id -> renderer PID+creationTime identity -> real CDP TargetID`;
- rejects synthetic `webcontents:<id>` target fallback for mutation authority;
- turns `AMBIGUOUS` working-memory state into a same-cell mutation barrier;
- makes renderer/WebContents death synchronously invalidate the runtime target before periodic reconciliation;
- reuses the existing persistent CDP session pool in `native-browser-control` instead of attach/detach-per semantic call;
- replaces the 20 x 100ms submit readback polling loop with an event-driven CDP outcome latch: subscribe before Enter, one race-closing read, event-triggered/coalesced follow-up reads, one bounded deadline, no automatic retry;
- documents read-only production findings and the server rollout design for transactional private `COMMAND_AVAILABLE` wake and durable mutation scopes.

## Important production findings

Read-only verification found two server constraints that are not changed by this PR:

1. live `h205f22_a2_browser_supervisor_issue_native_v1` inserts `PENDING` but does not call `realtime.send()`;
2. live `a2_browser_supervisor_one_mutating_inflight_uq` serializes all `PENDING/LEASED` mutating commands by `(workspace_id,target_client_id)`, so the DB currently permits only one mutating stream per Browser client;
3. deployed `a2-browser-native-supervisor-v1` is behind this repository branch and still exposes singular `/v1/commands/next`; the batch/wait-batch path in the repo is not yet the production path.

The design note proposes scope-safe evolution rather than deleting the global index: durable `READ | CELL | CLIENT_GLOBAL` scope, short transaction-level admission fencing, queue-style `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` lease selection, and same-scope/global-barrier causal ordering.

## Safety invariants

- production DDL/deployment: **not performed**;
- Browser actuation: **not performed**;
- wake transport is never authority;
- runtime control plane is not scheduler/lease authority;
- stale binding execution is fail-closed;
- `AMBIGUOUS` never triggers automatic effect retry;
- periodic process census is reconciliation/telemetry, not mutation authority.

## Validation

- syntax-checked the new runtime-control-plane module and its test locally with Node;
- added focused tests for exact target fencing, PID reuse/generation fencing, immediate renderer-death invalidation, `AMBIGUOUS` barrier, pressure non-authority, event-driven latch/no polling, burst coalescing and bounded ambiguous deadline;
- repository CI should provide full integration validation on the stacked branch.

## Follow-up wiring

This PR deliberately establishes the exact contract before final `main.mjs` execution-authority wiring. The next slice should feed `BrowserRealtimeProcessPlane` exact `tab_id` resolution into this plane, prepare the runtime fence for DB-leased tab effects, and assert it at the final physical mutation callsite so selected/platform fallback is impossible for remote mutation.

## Purpose
Let the existing Browser command scheduler use more of healthy 2026 hardware without turning overload into latency collapse.

## Changes
- add sample-driven `BrowserControlPressureGovernor` with GREEN/YELLOW/ORANGE/RED pressure bands;
- derive bounded concurrency from event-loop utilization/delay, renderer CPU, main-process memory, network inflight, lease/result RTT and crash/unresponsive signals;
- GREEN budget: up to 128 reads and 32 independent BrowserCell mutations; RED: 8 reads / 2 mutations;
- mutation budget never exceeds exact live-cell count;
- degradation is immediate, recovery is hysteretic and one band at a time;
- add bounded `setConcurrencyBudget()` to the existing command lane scheduler; no scheduler recreation or second timer;
- add pressure and scheduler integration regressions.

## Stack
Base: PR #331 branch `work/browser-brain-o1-scheduler-v1`.

## Authority boundary
Pressure changes capacity only. It cannot lease commands, execute Browser effects, change effect binding, retry ambiguous outcomes, merge, deploy, or release.

## Purpose
Remove repeated full-batch causal scans from the Browser command hot path while preserving the existing lane/effect authority model.

## Changes
- bump command-lane contract to v3;
- precompute per-causal-key read/mutation prefix ordinals once in O(n);
- replace `pending.some(...)` predecessor scans with O(1) comparisons against launched counters;
- preserve existing read fan-out, same-tab read/write causality, distinct-tab mutation overlap, global/emergency exclusivity and unknown-action fail-closed behavior;
- add a 256-command / 32-BrowserCell stress regression plus static proof that `pending.some` is absent from the hot path.

## Stack
Base: PR #330 branch `work/browser-brain-cell-binding-v1`.

## Authority boundary
- no new scheduler or timer;
- no DB/Edge/production changes;
- no command/effect authority changes;
- no merge/release/cutover;
- automatic effect retry remains forbidden.

## Purpose
Make the Browser Brain's live state exact enough for low-latency parallel control without creating a second scheduler or a new authority path.

## Changes
- add an O(1) runtime binding index: `tab_id -> WebContents.id -> renderer pid+creationTime -> CDP target_id`, with binding generations and immediate invalidation on renderer/WebContents loss;
- add bounded provider-neutral working memory for compact causal facts, command outcomes and hash-verified checkpoints;
- explicitly exclude page text, input values, raw DOM/network payloads and command/result payloads from working memory;
- keep both modules observation/memory-only: no command lease, execution authority, retry loop or Browser effect;
- add adversarial tests for PID reuse, stale binding fences, crash invalidation, AMBIGUOUS memory, checkpoint tamper detection and bounded rings.

## Stack
Base is exact green PR #329 head `a0da28a882960310df48d49f702c8b1b901da2fc` so cognitive ingest remains the parent transport contract.

## Non-goals / authority boundary
- no production DDL or Edge deployment;
- no Browser actuation;
- no merge/release/cutover in this PR;
- no widening of current DB lease/effect authority;
- no second polling loop or scheduler.

## Next slices after this contract is green
1. wire existing `BrowserRealtimeProcessPlane` into the exact binding index and working memory;
2. replace repeated scheduler `pending.some()` causal scans with O(1) predecessor bookkeeping while preserving global/emergency barriers;
3. add private Realtime command-ready wake as a transport hint only; the existing signed durable lease remains the sole execution authority;
4. move shell/brain deltas onto one long-lived `MessageChannelMain`, retaining full snapshots only for initial sync/gap recovery.

## Browser Brain / Cognitive Ingest V1

This is the next atomic step toward the 2026 technical ceiling for continuous Browser cognition: keep high-rate process/semantic deltas hot, durable and duplicate-safe without rebuilding `/v1/state` for every event or persisting an event ledger.

### What changes
- adds rollback-only `browser_cognitive_delta_ingest_v1.sql`;
- stores O(1) durable cursor state per exact `(workspace, client, device, stream)`;
- exact contiguous advance under `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`;
- ACK-loss duplicate replay is accepted without duplicate broadcast;
- gap/overlap is rejected with full-state resync required;
- one sanitized batch becomes one private `realtime.send` broadcast in the same DB transaction as cursor advancement;
- no page text, input values, raw CDP payload, command leasing or effect authority enters this path;
- DB does constant-cost boundary/fence validation instead of reparsing all projected events;
- adds Windows + Linux exact-head CI for stream/ACK/Edge/SQL contracts.

### Authority / cutover boundary
Source-only. This PR does **not** apply production DDL, deploy Edge, publish a Browser release, reset Browser state, issue Browser commands, or change command authority. DB command lease remains the only actuation authority. Cognitive Broadcast is observation delivery only.

### Performance intent
Healthy hot path is one authenticated HTTP batch -> one small cursor-row transaction -> one private Realtime broadcast. No per-event DB row, no fixed-delay timer, no second command scheduler, no automatic physical-effect retry.

Merge only after exact-head CI is terminal green and after review of the SQL source contract. Production graduation remains a separate explicit change window.

## Scope

Stacked hardening slice on canonical Sovereign Browser Compute Fabric foundation #304. Adds no live/production authority and does not mutate Supabase, Browser, WTS, SCM, release publication or current authority.

## Selective reconvergence

The duplicate #303 was closed as superseded. This PR selectively preserves only its useful supply-chain ideas while keeping #304's safer staging boundaries.

## Update trust hardening

Adds a pure TUF/OCI/SLSA/Sigstore-style evidence verifier that requires:
- root/targets/snapshot/timestamp role envelopes with independently verified signatures;
- role expiry and monotonic trusted version floors for rollback/freeze protection;
- verified root thresholds and root rotation evidence;
- snapshot -> targets and timestamp -> snapshot exact version + SHA-256 + byte-size bindings;
- exact artifact descriptor: SHA-256 + byte size + media type + source SHA;
- SLSA provenance bound to exact subject digest, byte size and source SHA;
- transparency proof bound to the same artifact;
- independent platform signature verification.

A raw Git SHA is never sufficient and the module is authority-effect-free.

## Verification

The Fabric workflow now runs the complete foundation plus update-trust adversarial suite on both `windows-2025` and `ubuntu-24.04`, checks the exact candidate HEAD, preserves source-only SQL boundaries and proves a clean checkout.

